--- Conclusion: family is parameterized by q on j-line via
    j(q) = 256 (1 - q^2 + q^4)^3 / (q^2 (1-q^2)^2)

This is the MODULAR CURVE X_0(N)/something. Let's check which one.

Recall the Legendre family E_lambda: y^2 = x(x-1)(x-lambda) has
    j(lambda) = 256 (1 - lambda + lambda^2)^3 / (lambda^2 (1-lambda)^2)

Substituting lambda = q^2:
    j(q^2) = 256 (1 - q^2 + q^4)^3 / (q^4 (1 - q^2)^2)

Compare: j(E_{m,n}) = 256 (1 - q^2 + q^4)^3 / (q^2 (1 - q^2)^2)

Ratio: j(E_{m,n}) / j(Legendre(q^2)) = q^2.
These are NOT equal. But our E_{m,n} is X(X+1)(X+q^2),
which is the Legendre form with lambda = -q^2 (shifted).

